INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-3f15bb2900','task-f471043f3e',1787386502.7403655,'{"task_id": "task-f471043f3e", "run_id": "run-3f15bb2900", "started_at": 1787386502.7403655, "finished_at": 1787391472.7843816, "status": "ok", "result_text": "Wrote **breakage-2026-08-22.md**. Key findings from the 2026-08-21 report onward:\n\n1. **llama.cpp v0.2.0** (2026-08-21) \u2014 first semver STABLE release of llama.cpp; the `vX.Y.Z` stable track starts here, `bNUM` continues as nightly. Vulkan-path changes are in the changelog I read, no HIP or gfx1151-specific break noted.\n2. **unsloth PR #5301** (str-strix halo and windows AMD ROCm support) \u2014 was open/merged-status unknown as of yesterday; **now confirmed MERGED** (danny-avila''s docs page also cites it as shipped).\n3. **ROCm busy-spin (TheRock #7051)** \u2014 still open; no new comments or fix since 2026-08-13; and the reporter''s affected-matrix explicitly includes the `whl-multi-arch/` 7.14 channel, so a production-wheel jump is **not** a clean escape from your top risk \u2014 the clean arm they measured is `rocm==7.2.x` production.\n\nEverything else (torch, transformers 5.15.1, ollama 0.32.15, OpenWorker v0.1.7, unsloth v0.1.801-beta, kernel 7.0-series) is unchanged from yesterday.\n\nOne honest caveat I left out of the list deliberately: **LibreChat (librechat-dev:latest)** \u2014 I could not verify its current version today because the GitHub API 404''d at both `danny-avila/LibreChat/releases` and `librechat/librechat/releases`. The GHCR namespace (`ghcr.io/danny-avila/librechat-dev`) is still the live image. I would not name a version or CVE I have not read directly. Next run should re-resolve the repo first (a possible re-org/rename) before making any claim.\n\nFile: `/home/iconbaypark2900/OpenWorker/__task__task-f471043f3e/breakage-2026-08-22.md`", "artifacts": ["breakage-2026-08-22.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-3f15bb2900"}');
