INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-7687c01ffc','task-1b2c4d3f13',1787385602.72070837,'{"task_id": "task-1b2c4d3f13", "run_id": "run-7687c01ffc", "started_at": 1787385602.7207084, "finished_at": 1787393924.6166325, "status": "ok", "result_text": "Done. `papers-2026-08-22.md` is written in the workspace.\n\nWhat I found, honestly caveated:\n\n- **The arXiv MCP snapshot reached today tops out at 2026-08-20 afternoon submissions** \u2014 so this run is effectively a 2-day-old surface, not a true 24-hour tail. I flagged that in the file''s header rather than papering over it. The arXiv listing page for 08-21 is rate-limiting me right now, and the tavily/exa gateways aren''t wired to this profile, so I couldn''t independently confirm whether 08-21/22 additions exist.\n- **Quantum computing \u2014 4 new-to-my-report items, all verified via abstract:** Kordonowy\u2013Watkins (sharp learnability cliff at d* \u2248 log\u2082n + log\u2082log\u2082n for all-to-all brickwork circuits \u2014 the learning-theoretic boundary behind circuit-learning crypto claims); Burov\u2013Javerzac (fan-out parallel compilation for Heisenberg/NMR Hamiltonians with built-in post-selection, with the win conditional on 1\u20131.5 orders better error rates); Li et al. (single-basis entanglement-structure classification, >95% up to 100 qubits sim, validated to 13 qubits on hardware); Patil et al. (a \"higher Nishimori\" tricritical point in Potts-model learning / monitored-deformed Zq toric codes \u2014 the cleanest QEC-meets-inference bridge this month).\n- **Machine learning \u2014 1 verified new item:** Kulkarni et al.''s cache-eviction audit, whose real finding is the negative one \u2014 no policy beats LFU by more than 0.041 points, and only 2.1\u20133.9% of semantic-cache hits are actually answer-substitutable.\n- **Recursive self-improvement \u2014 nothing new.** The 08-21 items (AI4AI-Bench, Phantom Gains, EnvHarness) still stand and I carried them forward as live priors; the only RSI paper in today''s snapshot I could verify (HELIX, 2026-08-14) predates the window.\n- Continuity: Eureka''s unverified math claim stays open, and the Blanc/Liu\u2013Mutreja structure-or-depth line is treated as converged for the window.\n\nOne thing worth acting on: before re-sharing this file, do a same-day arXiv re-pull for 08-21/22 \u2014 I''d rather miss a first-day paper than miscite an ID, and I''d rather re-flag it tomorrow than pad today''s list with unverified ones.", "artifacts": ["papers-2026-08-22.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "session_id": "__run__run-7687c01ffc"}');
