INSERT INTO task_runs VALUES('run-323e6f76c9','task-db9b445c7a',1787556621.28488349,'{"task_id": "task-db9b445c7a", "run_id": "run-323e6f76c9", "started_at": 1787556621.2848835, "finished_at": 1787557542.1181755, "status": "ok", "result_text": "Done. Here''s what the evidence actually showed and what I wrote.\n\n**Key finding vs. last week''s file:** big state change \u2014 openEvolve moved from \"Phase 2 in flight\" to **Phase 3 active**. Phase 2 is fully closed (4/4 items, 71 tests, per `PHASE2.md`), and you''ve been grinding Phase 3 all of 08-22\u219224 (five builder sessions of 231/322/367/274/54 messages). The \"what replaces the surrogate-offline docking proxy\" open question is **resolved** \u2014 the Vina adapter shipped (`2529fa0`) and, per the brain thread, the SMILES\u2192PDBQT seam (`6f71a30`) closed too. What''s genuinely stuck now: **live-docking can''t run on this host** \u2014 no vina binary, no meeko/OpenBabel \u2014 so the fake-vina harness is the only proof of the real path.\n\n**Active (5, ranked by evidence):** openEvolve/Phase 3 \u2192 OpenWorker app itself (20+ commits 08-22/23 on MCP-tool grants + honest run-stop markers) \u2192 job/grant pipeline (unchanged open question: 37 drafts, *nothing sent*) \u2192 workstation-stack (edge of window, last commit 08-21) \u2192 research corpus (standing watch, 2 papers this week).\n\n**Quiet:** dcode-stack (last 2026-08-16, 8 days untouched) and the Sigma market brief (disabled since 08-15) \u2014 carried over, not deleted. **Parked:** left verbatim (empty, as was).\n\n**Distribution:** copied to canonical `OpenWorker/knowledge/FOCUS.md` + all **149** task workspaces, verified `149/149` \u2014 matches the workspace count exactly, no shortfall. llama.cpp and LibreChat explicitly excluded as upstream clones (authorship: Gerganov/Avila, not you).\n\nReport file: `FOCUS.md` in both your scratch workspace and `~/OpenWorker/knowledge/`.", "artifacts": ["FOCUS.md"], "error": null, "trigger": "schedule", "sessio